module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.Fibres.BertiniChartSupport
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.Fibres.BertiniCommonZeroSet
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.Fibres.BertiniFlatFamily

/-!
# The open of parameters whose divisor avoids a rational point

Work in the standing situation of the Bertini theorems ([Stacks, Tag 0G47]). The proof of
[Stacks, Tag 0FD6] needs a nonempty open `U ⊂ 𝔸^r_k` of the parameter space over which no fibre
of `q : H_univ → 𝔸^r_k` contains an irreducible component of `X`. The construction of the source
is: for each irreducible component `X'` of `X` pick a closed point `x' ∈ X'` and take the
parameters `v` with `ψ(v)(x') ≠ 0`; after the reduction to an algebraically closed base field
this is the basic open `D(∑ᵢ cᵢxᵢ)` of `𝔸^r_k`, with `cᵢ = fᵢ(x')` the values at `x'` of the
functions representing `ψ(v₁), …, ψ(v_r)` on a trivializing chart.

This module carries out that construction for one `k`-rational point of `X`.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Bertini.FamilyDivisors.rationalPointSection` is the section `σ_x : 𝔸^r_k → 𝔸^r_X` of
  the projection `𝔸^r_X → 𝔸^r_k` determined by a `k`-point `x` of `X`.
* `Stacks.Bertini.FamilyDivisors.rationalPointCoeff` is the value `cᵢ = fᵢ(x)` and
  `Stacks.Bertini.FamilyDivisors.rationalPointLinearForm` is the function `∑ᵢ cᵢxᵢ` on `𝔸^r_k`.
* `Stacks.Bertini.FamilyDivisors.rationalPointOpen` is the basic open `D(∑ᵢ cᵢxᵢ) ⊂ 𝔸^r_k`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Bertini.FamilyDivisors.ideal_universalDivisor_comap_rationalPointSection`: the
  universal divisor pulled back along `σ_x` is cut out on `𝔸^r_k` by `∑ᵢ cᵢxᵢ`.
* `Stacks.Bertini.FamilyDivisors.mem_rationalPointOpen_iff`: a parameter lies in the open
  exactly when `σ_x` carries it outside the universal divisor.
* `Stacks.Bertini.FamilyDivisors.nonempty_rationalPointOpen`: the open is nonempty as soon as
  one of the values `cᵢ` is nonzero, that is, as soon as the linear system does not vanish
  identically at `x`.
* `Stacks.Bertini.FamilyDivisors.not_fibre_subset_supportSet_of_mem_rationalPointOpen`: no
  fibre of `𝔸^r_X → 𝔸^r_k` over the open is contained in the universal divisor.
* `Stacks.Bertini.FamilyDivisors.universalSection_fibre_ne_zero` and
  `Stacks.Bertini.FamilyDivisors.universalSection_restrict_fibre_ne_zero`: the universal section
  therefore restricts to a nonzero section on each such fibre; the second is the shape consumed
  by `Stacks.Bertini.FamilyDivisors.flat_universalDivisor_restrict_of_fibres_isIntegral`.
* `Stacks.Bertini.FamilyDivisors.exists_rationalPointCoeff_ne_zero_of_notMem_commonZeroSet`: a
  `k`-point outside the common zero locus `Z = ⋂_{v ∈ V} H_v` of the linear system has a nonzero
  coefficient, so its open is nonempty. This is the link from the generation hypothesis of
  [Stacks, Tag 0FD6] to the chart equations.
* `Stacks.Bertini.FamilyDivisors.exists_notMem_supportSet_over_rationalPoint`: over every
  parameter of the open the fibre of `𝔸^r_X → 𝔸^r_k` contains a point above the chosen `k`-point
  of `X` and outside `H_univ`.
* `Stacks.Bertini.FamilyDivisors.nonempty_finsetInf_parameterBase`: a finite intersection of
  nonempty opens of `𝔸^r_k` is nonempty, which is how the opens of one point in each irreducible
  component of `X` are combined. The components are finitely many because `X` is of finite type
  over `k`, hence a Noetherian space; that is
  `TopologicalSpace.NoetherianSpace.finite_irreducibleComponents`.

## Implementation notes

A `k`-point of `X` landing in a trivializing affine open `U = Spec A` is recorded as a morphism
`x₀ : Spec k → U`, so that the values `cᵢ = x₀^#(fᵢ)` of the chart equations at it are available
with no further factoring; the point of `X` itself is `x₀ ≫ U.ι`, and the section of
`𝔸^r_X → 𝔸^r_k` it determines is `AlgebraicGeometry.AffineSpace.map` applied to it. That the
composite `𝔸^r_k → 𝔸^r_X → 𝔸^r_k` is the identity is the functoriality of relative affine space
applied to the identity `x ≫ (X → Spec k) = 𝟙`, which is the hypothesis that `x` is a point
*over* `k`.

The local equation of `σ_x^{-1}H_univ` is computed from the local equation of `H_univ` on the
chart `𝔸^r_U` (`Stacks.Bertini.FamilyDivisors.universalDivisor_comap_chartMap`) by one further
pullback along `𝔸^r_k → 𝔸^r_U`, since `σ_x` factors through the chart. The resulting ideal of
`Γ(𝔸^r_k, ⊤)` is principal, generated by `∑ᵢ cᵢxᵢ`, and `𝔸^r_k` is a reduced affine scheme, so
the complementary basic open is nonempty exactly when that function is nonzero; the function is
read in the polynomial ring `k[x₁, …, x_r]` by `AlgebraicGeometry.AffineSpace.ΓIso`, where it is
visibly nonzero as soon as one coefficient is.

What the source does and this module does not is produce the rational point: over a general
base field a closed point of `X` has a residue field larger than `k`, and the source removes
this by base changing to an algebraic closure. Here the `k`-point is an input.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FD6](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FD6)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0G47](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0G47)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits TopologicalSpace Opposite

universe u v

namespace Stacks.Bertini.FamilyDivisors

variable (D : FamilyDivisors.{u, v})

/-! ### The section of the parameter space over a rational point -/

/-- The projection `𝔸^r_k → Spec k` of the parameter space of the base field. -/
abbrev parameterBaseProjection : D.parameterBase ⟶ Spec (.of D.k) :=
  𝔸(D.basisIndex; Spec (.of D.k)) ↘ Spec (.of D.k)

/-- **The section `σ_x : 𝔸^r_k → 𝔸^r_X`** of the projection `𝔸^r_X → 𝔸^r_k` determined by a
`k`-point `x` of `X`. -/
def rationalPointSection (x : Spec (.of D.k) ⟶ D.X) : D.parameterBase ⟶ D.parameterSpace :=
  AffineSpace.map D.basisIndex x

/-- **`σ_x` is a section of `𝔸^r_X → 𝔸^r_k`** when `x` is a point of `X` over `k`. -/
theorem rationalPointSection_comp_parameterBaseMap (x : Spec (.of D.k) ⟶ D.X)
    (hx : x ≫ D.toBase = 𝟙 (Spec (.of D.k))) :
    D.rationalPointSection x ≫ D.parameterBaseMap = 𝟙 D.parameterBase := by
  change AffineSpace.map D.basisIndex x ≫ AffineSpace.map D.basisIndex D.toBase = _
  rw [← AffineSpace.map_comp, hx, AffineSpace.map_id]

/-- The image of a parameter under the section lies over it. -/
theorem parameterBaseMap_rationalPointSection (x : Spec (.of D.k) ⟶ D.X)
    (hx : x ≫ D.toBase = 𝟙 (Spec (.of D.k))) (u : D.parameterBase) :
    D.parameterBaseMap.base ((D.rationalPointSection x).base u) = u := by
  have h := congrArg (fun m : D.parameterBase ⟶ D.parameterBase => m.base u)
    (D.rationalPointSection_comp_parameterBaseMap x hx)
  simpa using h

/-! ### The local equation of the universal divisor along the section -/

variable {D} {U : D.X.Opens}

/-- The value `cᵢ = fᵢ(x)` at a `k`-point of a trivializing chart of the function representing
`ψ(vᵢ)` there. -/
def rationalPointCoeff
    (eU : D.restrictedModule U ≅ SheafOfModules.unit U.toScheme.ringCatSheaf)
    (x₀ : Spec (.of D.k) ⟶ U.toScheme) (i : Fin (Module.finrank D.k D.V)) :
    Γ(Spec (.of D.k), ⊤) :=
  x₀.appTop (D.chartEquation eU i)

/-- **The linear form `∑ᵢ cᵢxᵢ`** on `𝔸^r_k` cut out by a `k`-point of a trivializing chart. -/
def rationalPointLinearForm
    (eU : D.restrictedModule U ≅ SheafOfModules.unit U.toScheme.ringCatSheaf)
    (x₀ : Spec (.of D.k) ⟶ U.toScheme) : Γ(D.parameterBase, ⊤) :=
  ∑ i, AffineSpace.coord (Spec (.of D.k)) (ULift.up i) *
    D.parameterBaseProjection.appTop (rationalPointCoeff eU x₀ i)

/-- **The universal divisor pulled back along the section of a `k`-point of a chart.** It is the
zero scheme on `𝔸^r_k` of `∑ᵢ xᵢ · ψ(vᵢ)|_U`, pulled back along `𝔸^r_k → Spec k → U`. -/
theorem universalDivisor_comap_rationalPointSection (x₀ : Spec (.of D.k) ⟶ U.toScheme) :
    D.universalDivisor.comap (D.rationalPointSection (x₀ ≫ U.ι)) =
      zeroScheme D.parameterBase
        ((Scheme.Modules.pullback (D.parameterBaseProjection ≫ x₀)).obj (D.restrictedModule U))
        (∑ i, AffineSpace.coord (Spec (.of D.k)) (ULift.up i) •
          pullbackGlobalSections (D.parameterBaseProjection ≫ x₀) (D.restrictedModule U)
            (D.restrictedSection U (D.basis i))) := by
  let := D.isInvertible
  have hp : AffineSpace.map D.basisIndex x₀ ≫ D.chartProjection U =
      D.parameterBaseProjection ≫ x₀ := AffineSpace.map_over x₀
  have hcoord : ∀ i : Fin (Module.finrank D.k D.V),
      (AffineSpace.map D.basisIndex x₀).appTop (AffineSpace.coord U.toScheme (ULift.up i)) =
        AffineSpace.coord (Spec (.of D.k)) (ULift.up i) :=
    fun i => AffineSpace.map_appTop_coord _ _
  have h := zeroScheme_sum_smul_comap (D.restrictedModule U) (D.chartProjection U)
    (AffineSpace.map D.basisIndex x₀) (D.parameterBaseProjection ≫ x₀) hp
    (fun i => AffineSpace.coord U.toScheme (ULift.up i))
    (fun i => AffineSpace.coord (Spec (.of D.k)) (ULift.up i)) hcoord
    (fun i => D.restrictedSection U (D.basis i))
  rw [h, ← D.universalDivisor_comap_chartMap U, ← Scheme.IdealSheafData.comap_comp]
  change _ = D.universalDivisor.comap (AffineSpace.map D.basisIndex x₀ ≫ D.chartMap U)
  rw [chartMap, ← AffineSpace.map_comp]
  rfl

/-- **The universal divisor is cut out on `𝔸^r_k` by `∑ᵢ cᵢxᵢ` along the section of a
`k`-point.** -/
theorem ideal_universalDivisor_comap_rationalPointSection
    (eU : D.restrictedModule U ≅ SheafOfModules.unit U.toScheme.ringCatSheaf)
    (x₀ : Spec (.of D.k) ⟶ U.toScheme) :
    (D.universalDivisor.comap (D.rationalPointSection (x₀ ≫ U.ι))).ideal
        ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top D.parameterBase⟩ =
      Ideal.span {rationalPointLinearForm eU x₀} := by
  let := D.isInvertible
  rw [D.universalDivisor_comap_rationalPointSection x₀]
  refine (Stacks.Divisors.zeroScheme_ideal_top_sum_smul (D.parameterBaseProjection ≫ x₀)
    (D.restrictedModule U) eU (fun i => AffineSpace.coord (Spec (.of D.k)) (ULift.up i))
    (fun i => D.restrictedSection U (D.basis i))).trans ?_
  congr 1

/-! ### The basic open of the linear form -/

/-- **The open `D(∑ᵢ cᵢxᵢ) ⊂ 𝔸^r_k`** of parameters whose divisor avoids the `k`-point. -/
def rationalPointOpen
    (eU : D.restrictedModule U ≅ SheafOfModules.unit U.toScheme.ringCatSheaf)
    (x₀ : Spec (.of D.k) ⟶ U.toScheme) : D.parameterBase.Opens :=
  D.parameterBase.basicOpen (rationalPointLinearForm eU x₀)

/-- The linear form `∑ᵢ cᵢxᵢ`, read in the polynomial ring `k[x₁, …, x_r]`. -/
theorem ΓIso_hom_rationalPointLinearForm
    (eU : D.restrictedModule U ≅ SheafOfModules.unit U.toScheme.ringCatSheaf)
    (x₀ : Spec (.of D.k) ⟶ U.toScheme) :
    (AffineSpace.ΓIso D.basisIndex (Spec (.of D.k))).hom (rationalPointLinearForm eU x₀) =
      ∑ i, MvPolynomial.C (rationalPointCoeff eU x₀ i) * MvPolynomial.X (ULift.up i) := by
  rw [rationalPointLinearForm, map_sum]
  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ => ?_
  rw [map_mul, AffineSpace.ΓIso_hom_coord, AffineSpace.ΓIso_hom_appTop, mul_comm]

/-- **The linear form is nonzero** as soon as one of the values `cᵢ = fᵢ(x)` is. -/
theorem rationalPointLinearForm_ne_zero
    (eU : D.restrictedModule U ≅ SheafOfModules.unit U.toScheme.ringCatSheaf)
    (x₀ : Spec (.of D.k) ⟶ U.toScheme) {i₀ : Fin (Module.finrank D.k D.V)}
    (h : rationalPointCoeff eU x₀ i₀ ≠ 0) :
    rationalPointLinearForm eU x₀ ≠ 0 := by
  classical
  intro hzero
  refine h ?_
  have hpoly := ΓIso_hom_rationalPointLinearForm eU x₀
  rw [hzero, map_zero] at hpoly
  have hc := congrArg (MvPolynomial.coeffAddMonoidHom (Finsupp.single (ULift.up i₀) 1)) hpoly
  simp only [map_zero, MvPolynomial.coeffAddMonoidHom_apply] at hc
  rw [MvPolynomial.coeff_sum,
    Finset.sum_eq_single_of_mem i₀ (Finset.mem_univ i₀) ?_] at hc
  · rw [MvPolynomial.coeff_C_mul, MvPolynomial.coeff_X_same, mul_one] at hc
    exact hc.symm
  · intro b _ hb
    rw [MvPolynomial.coeff_C_mul, MvPolynomial.coeff_X, ite_eq_right, mul_zero]
    intro hcon
    exact hb (congrArg ULift.down (Finsupp.single_left_injective one_ne_zero hcon))

/-- **The open `D(∑ᵢ cᵢxᵢ)` is nonempty** as soon as the linear system does not vanish
identically at the `k`-point. -/
theorem nonempty_rationalPointOpen
    (eU : D.restrictedModule U ≅ SheafOfModules.unit U.toScheme.ringCatSheaf)
    (x₀ : Spec (.of D.k) ⟶ U.toScheme) {i₀ : Fin (Module.finrank D.k D.V)}
    (h : rationalPointCoeff eU x₀ i₀ ≠ 0) :
    ((rationalPointOpen eU x₀ : D.parameterBase.Opens) : Set D.parameterBase).Nonempty := by
  let := D.isField
  by_contra hne
  rw [TopologicalSpace.Opens.not_nonempty_iff_eq_bot, rationalPointOpen,
    AlgebraicGeometry.basicOpen_eq_bot_iff] at hne
  exact rationalPointLinearForm_ne_zero eU x₀ h hne

/-- A point lies in the support of the pullback of an ideal sheaf iff its image lies in the
support of the ideal sheaf. -/
private theorem mem_supportSet_comap_iff {Y Z : Scheme.{u}} (I : Y.IdealSheafData) (g : Z ⟶ Y)
    (z : Z) : z ∈ (I.comap g).supportSet ↔ g.base z ∈ I.supportSet := by
  rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.mem_supportSet_iff_mem_support,
    Scheme.IdealSheafData.mem_supportSet_iff_mem_support, Scheme.IdealSheafData.support_comap]
  exact Iff.rfl

/-- **A parameter lies in the open exactly when the section carries it outside the universal
divisor.** -/
theorem mem_rationalPointOpen_iff
    (eU : D.restrictedModule U ≅ SheafOfModules.unit U.toScheme.ringCatSheaf)
    (x₀ : Spec (.of D.k) ⟶ U.toScheme) (u : D.parameterBase) :
    u ∈ rationalPointOpen eU x₀ ↔
      (D.rationalPointSection (x₀ ≫ U.ι)).base u ∉ D.universalDivisor.supportSet := by
  rw [← mem_supportSet_comap_iff, Scheme.IdealSheafData.mem_supportSet_iff_of_mem
      (U := ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top D.parameterBase⟩) (by trivial),
    ideal_universalDivisor_comap_rationalPointSection eU x₀, Scheme.zeroLocus_span,
    Scheme.zeroLocus_singleton]
  simp [rationalPointOpen]

/-! ### No fibre over the open lies in the universal divisor -/

variable (D) in
/-- **No fibre of `𝔸^r_X → 𝔸^r_k` over the open is contained in the universal divisor.** The
section of a `k`-point carries a parameter of the open to a point of its fibre outside
`H_univ`. -/
theorem not_fibre_subset_supportSet_of_mem_rationalPointOpen
    (eU : D.restrictedModule U ≅ SheafOfModules.unit U.toScheme.ringCatSheaf)
    (x₀ : Spec (.of D.k) ⟶ U.toScheme)
    (hx : (x₀ ≫ U.ι) ≫ D.toBase = 𝟙 (Spec (.of D.k)))
    (u : D.parameterBase) (hu : u ∈ rationalPointOpen eU x₀) :
    ¬ (D.parameterBaseMap.base ⁻¹' {u} ⊆ D.universalDivisor.supportSet) := by
  intro hsub
  refine (mem_rationalPointOpen_iff eU x₀ u).mp hu (hsub ?_)
  exact D.parameterBaseMap_rationalPointSection (x₀ ≫ U.ι) hx u

/-- **A section of an invertible module whose zero scheme misses a point of the source is
nonzero.** -/
theorem _root_.Stacks.Divisors.ne_zero_of_notMem_supportSet_comap {Y Z : Scheme.{u}}
    (M : Y.Modules)
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible Y.sheaf.obj Y.ringCatSheaf.property M]
    (s : Γ(M, ⊤)) (g : Z ⟶ Y) {z : Z} (hz : g.base z ∉ (zeroScheme Y M s).supportSet) :
    pullbackGlobalSections g M s ≠ 0 := by
  intro hs
  have hsupp : z ∈ ((zeroScheme Y M s).comap g).supportSet := by
    rw [← Stacks.Divisors.zeroScheme_pullback g M s, hs]
    have hbot : Stacks.Divisors.zeroScheme Z ((Scheme.Modules.pullback g).obj M) 0 = ⊥ := by
      ext V
      rw [Stacks.Divisors.zeroScheme_ideal]
      simp
    rw [hbot, Scheme.IdealSheafData.mem_supportSet_iff_mem_support,
      Scheme.IdealSheafData.support_bot]
    trivial
  exact hz ((mem_supportSet_comap_iff _ g z).1 hsupp)

variable (D) in
/-- **The universal section restricts to a nonzero section on every fibre over the open.** -/
theorem universalSection_fibre_ne_zero
    (eU : D.restrictedModule U ≅ SheafOfModules.unit U.toScheme.ringCatSheaf)
    (x₀ : Spec (.of D.k) ⟶ U.toScheme)
    (hx : (x₀ ≫ U.ι) ≫ D.toBase = 𝟙 (Spec (.of D.k)))
    (u : D.parameterBase) (hu : u ∈ rationalPointOpen eU x₀) :
    pullbackGlobalSections (D.parameterBaseMap.fiberι u)
      ((Scheme.Modules.pullback D.parameterProjection).obj D.L) D.universalSection ≠ 0 := by
  let := D.isInvertible
  have hmem : (D.rationalPointSection (x₀ ≫ U.ι)).base u ∈
      Set.range (D.parameterBaseMap.fiberι u).base := by
    rw [Scheme.Hom.range_fiberι]
    exact D.parameterBaseMap_rationalPointSection (x₀ ≫ U.ι) hx u
  obtain ⟨z, hz⟩ := hmem
  refine Stacks.Divisors.ne_zero_of_notMem_supportSet_comap
    ((Scheme.Modules.pullback D.parameterProjection).obj D.L) D.universalSection
    (D.parameterBaseMap.fiberι u) (z := z) ?_
  rw [hz]
  exact (mem_rationalPointOpen_iff eU x₀ u).mp hu

variable (D) in
/-- **The universal section restricts to a nonzero section on every fibre of `𝔸^r_X|_U → U`**,
in the shape consumed by
`Stacks.Bertini.FamilyDivisors.flat_universalDivisor_restrict_of_fibres_isIntegral`. -/
theorem universalSection_restrict_fibre_ne_zero
    (eU : D.restrictedModule U ≅ SheafOfModules.unit U.toScheme.ringCatSheaf)
    (x₀ : Spec (.of D.k) ⟶ U.toScheme)
    (hx : (x₀ ≫ U.ι) ≫ D.toBase = 𝟙 (Spec (.of D.k)))
    (u : (rationalPointOpen eU x₀ : D.parameterBase.Opens)) :
    pullbackGlobalSections
        ((D.parameterBaseMap ∣_ rationalPointOpen eU x₀).fiberι u ≫
          (D.restrictedParameterSpace (rationalPointOpen eU x₀)).ι)
        ((Scheme.Modules.pullback D.parameterProjection).obj D.L) D.universalSection ≠ 0 := by
  let := D.isInvertible
  have hbase : D.parameterBaseMap.base ((D.rationalPointSection (x₀ ≫ U.ι)).base u.1) = u.1 :=
    D.parameterBaseMap_rationalPointSection (x₀ ≫ U.ι) hx u.1
  have hmem : (D.rationalPointSection (x₀ ≫ U.ι)).base u.1 ∈
      D.parameterBaseMap ⁻¹ᵁ rationalPointOpen eU x₀ := by
    change D.parameterBaseMap.base _ ∈ rationalPointOpen eU x₀
    rw [hbase]
    exact u.2
  have hfib : (D.parameterBaseMap ∣_ rationalPointOpen eU x₀).base ⟨_, hmem⟩ = u :=
    Subtype.ext ((morphismRestrict_base_coe _ _ _).trans hbase)
  obtain ⟨z, hz⟩ :=
    ((D.parameterBaseMap ∣_ rationalPointOpen eU x₀).range_fiberι u).ge hfib
  refine Stacks.Divisors.ne_zero_of_notMem_supportSet_comap
    ((Scheme.Modules.pullback D.parameterProjection).obj D.L) D.universalSection _ (z := z) ?_
  rw [Scheme.Hom.comp_apply, hz]
  exact (mem_rationalPointOpen_iff eU x₀ u.1).mp u.2

/-! ### The rational point is not a base point -/

/-- **At a `k`-point outside the common zero locus some coefficient `cᵢ` is nonzero.**

This is the link between the generation hypothesis of [Stacks, Tag 0FD6] — the image of `ψ`
generates `L`, so the common zero locus `Z = ⋂_{v ∈ V} H_v` is empty — and the chart equations
`f₁, …, f_r`: the function of *any* vector of the linear system lies in the ideal generated by
the `fᵢ` (`Stacks.Bertini.FamilyDivisors.chartFunction_mem_span_chartEquation`), so if every
`fᵢ` vanished at the point then so would every `ψ(v)`, putting the point in `Z`. -/
theorem exists_rationalPointCoeff_ne_zero_of_notMem_commonZeroSet [IsAffine U.toScheme]
    (eU : D.restrictedModule U ≅ SheafOfModules.unit U.toScheme.ringCatSheaf)
    (x₀ : Spec (.of D.k) ⟶ U.toScheme) (p : Spec (.of D.k))
    (hx : U.ι.base (x₀.base p) ∉ D.commonZeroSet) :
    ∃ i, rationalPointCoeff eU x₀ i ≠ 0 := by
  by_contra hall
  push Not at hall
  refine hx (Set.mem_iInter.2 fun w => ?_)
  rw [mem_divisorSet_iff eU w (x₀.base p), Scheme.mem_zeroLocus_iff]
  rintro f (rfl : f = chartFunction eU w)
  have hsub : Set.range (D.chartEquation eU) ⊆
      (RingHom.ker (Scheme.Hom.appTop x₀).hom : Set Γ(U.toScheme, ⊤)) := by
    rintro _ ⟨i, rfl⟩
    exact RingHom.mem_ker.mpr (hall i)
  have hker : (Scheme.Hom.appTop x₀).hom (chartFunction eU w) = 0 :=
    RingHom.mem_ker.mp (Ideal.span_le.mpr hsub (chartFunction_mem_span_chartEquation eU w))
  intro hmem
  have hp : p ∈ (Spec (.of D.k)).basicOpen (x₀.appTop (chartFunction eU w)) := by
    rw [← Scheme.preimage_basicOpen_top]
    exact hmem
  rw [show x₀.appTop (chartFunction eU w) = 0 from hker, Scheme.basicOpen_zero] at hp
  exact hp

/-! ### The point of the fibre that the section produces -/

variable (D) in
/-- The section of a `k`-point of `X` lands over that point. -/
theorem parameterProjection_rationalPointSection (x : Spec (.of D.k) ⟶ D.X)
    (u : D.parameterBase) :
    D.parameterProjection.base ((D.rationalPointSection x).base u) =
      x.base (D.parameterBaseProjection.base u) := by
  rw [rationalPointSection, ← Scheme.Hom.comp_apply, AffineSpace.map_over,
    Scheme.Hom.comp_apply]

variable (D) in
/-- **Over every parameter of the open the fibre contains a point above the chosen `k`-point of
`X` that is outside the universal divisor.** This is the assertion that no fibre of
`q : H_univ → 𝔸^r_k` over the open contains the irreducible component of `X` through that
point. -/
theorem exists_notMem_supportSet_over_rationalPoint
    (eU : D.restrictedModule U ≅ SheafOfModules.unit U.toScheme.ringCatSheaf)
    (x₀ : Spec (.of D.k) ⟶ U.toScheme)
    (hx : (x₀ ≫ U.ι) ≫ D.toBase = 𝟙 (Spec (.of D.k)))
    (u : D.parameterBase) (hu : u ∈ rationalPointOpen eU x₀) :
    ∃ z : D.parameterSpace, D.parameterBaseMap.base z = u ∧
      D.parameterProjection.base z =
        U.ι.base (x₀.base (D.parameterBaseProjection.base u)) ∧
      z ∉ D.universalDivisor.supportSet := by
  refine ⟨(D.rationalPointSection (x₀ ≫ U.ι)).base u,
    D.parameterBaseMap_rationalPointSection (x₀ ≫ U.ι) hx u, ?_,
    (mem_rationalPointOpen_iff eU x₀ u).mp hu⟩
  rw [D.parameterProjection_rationalPointSection (x₀ ≫ U.ι) u]
  rfl

/-! ### Intersecting the opens of finitely many rational points -/

variable (D) in
/-- **A finite intersection of nonempty opens of `𝔸^r_k` is nonempty**, because the parameter
space is irreducible. This is what combines the opens of one `k`-point in each of the finitely
many irreducible components of `X` into a single nonempty open. The same argument for a family
indexed by a finite type is `exists_mem_iInter_of_irreducibleSpace`, which this does not use
because that lemma lives in the group-scheme part of the library. -/
theorem nonempty_finsetInf_parameterBase (S : Finset D.parameterBase.Opens)
    (hS : ∀ W ∈ S, ((W : D.parameterBase.Opens) : Set D.parameterBase).Nonempty) :
    ((S.inf id : D.parameterBase.Opens) : Set D.parameterBase).Nonempty := by
  have := D.irreducibleSpace_parameterBase
  classical
  induction S using Finset.induction with
  | empty =>
    simp
  | insert W S _ ih =>
    rw [Finset.inf_insert]
    obtain ⟨y, -, hy⟩ := (IrreducibleSpace.isIrreducible_univ D.parameterBase).2
      (W : Set D.parameterBase) ((S.inf id : D.parameterBase.Opens) : Set D.parameterBase)
      W.isOpen (S.inf id).isOpen
      (let ⟨y, hy⟩ := hS W (Finset.mem_insert_self W S); ⟨y, trivial, hy⟩)
      (let ⟨y, hy⟩ := ih fun V hV => hS V (Finset.mem_insert_of_mem hV); ⟨y, trivial, hy⟩)
    exact ⟨y, hy⟩

end Stacks.Bertini.FamilyDivisors

end
